   "quote": "We must conceive a surrounding splendor, proceeding indeed from this cause, but from it in a permanent state, like a light from the sun shining",
   "says": "Plotinus: what proceeds from the first is like light shining from the sun, the cause abiding unmoved."
  },
  {
   "concept": "soul",
   "source": "plotinus-taylor-1817",
   "quote": "yet it is a certain image of intellect",
